## Instructions
1. Start by finding and reading `hiera.yaml` (or `hiera.yml`) in each root path listed above — check the root itself and up to 3 parent directories. This file defines the hierarchy structure (v3 or v5 format) and tells you where data files live and their priority order.
2. Based on what you find in hiera.yaml, identify the data directories and hierarchy levels
3. Use `grep_file` to search for the lookup keys across the hiera data directories
4. Read the files that contain matches to understand the full variable definitions
5. Also read common.yaml (or equivalent base-level file) if it exists — it often contains lookup_options and default values that affect all levels
6. After exploring all relevant files, provide a comprehensive summary of:
   - The hiera hierarchy structure you discovered (version, levels, priorities)
   - Which files contain which lookup keys
   - The variable types and values found
   - Any encrypted values (ENC[PKCS7,...])
   - Merge strategies (lookup_options sections)
   - Cross-level overrides (same key defined at multiple levels)
   - Mapping recommendations for Ansible variable files
